IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-core`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019 (ACT) -- the defined benefits, from the seat of the individual.
--
-- SEAT: the person injured in a motor accident in the ACT; and, after a death, a dependant of the person who died, the
-- personal representative, or the person who has paid, or is liable to pay, the funeral expenses. "Can I apply, and
-- by when? Has the insurer accepted my application? Am I entitled to income replacement benefits, how much a fortnight
-- and until when? How much does my WPI give me, and can I sue? What death and funeral benefits are payable?" Every
-- question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in mai-core.l4;
-- this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same name mean the
-- same thing in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- FIGURES: the AWE indexed amounts of NI2026-402: for ss 96, 97 and 103, 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027; for ss 167,
-- 174 and 181, 1 April 2026 to 30 September 2027. Another day answers `not covered`.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Injuries Act 2019 (ACT) -- the injured person's, dependant's and funeral payer's questions`

-- The s 43 to s 50 limitations, from plain answers. A question passes FALSE for a limitation that does not bear on
-- the benefit it asks about (the core reads only the ones in that benefit's "subject to" list).
GIVEN `uninsured, no s 43 (2) exception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `uninsured, no s 43 (3) exception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one driving offence`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `two driving offences`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `self-inflicted`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `detainee`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `serious offence`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `terrorism`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `workers compensation accepted`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Division 2.2.2 facts`
`my division 2.2.2 facts` `uninsured, no s 43 (2) exception` `uninsured, no s 43 (3) exception` `one driving offence` `two driving offences` `self-inflicted` `detainee` `serious offence` `terrorism` `workers compensation accepted` MEANS
    `Division 2.2.2 facts` WITH
        `s 43 (2): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS `uninsured, no s 43 (2) exception`
        `s 43 (3): driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle, with no other insured vehicle whose insurer is the relevant insurer` IS `uninsured, no s 43 (3) exception`
        `s 44: convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident` IS `one driving offence` OR `two driving offences`
        `s 45: convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident` IS `two driving offences`
        `s 46: the injury is intentionally self-inflicted` IS `self-inflicted`
        `s 47: a detainee or young detainee for the period` IS `detainee`
        `s 48: convicted or found guilty of a serious offence in relation to the accident` IS `serious offence`
        `s 49: the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS `terrorism`
        `s 50: a workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS `workers compensation accepted`

-- The injured person's facts. The person asking is alive (s 91 is for the estate's questions, s 175).
GIVEN `accident`       IS A DATE
      `age`            IS A NUMBER
      `situation`      IS A `Work situation`
      `pension age`    IS A DATE
      `damages paid`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitations` IS A `Division 2.2.2 facts`
GIVETH AN `Injured person's facts`
`my facts as an injured person` `accident` `age` `situation` `pension age` `damages paid` `the limitations` MEANS
    `Injured person's facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                       IS `accident`
        `age on the date of the motor accident`            IS `age`
        `work situation on the date of the motor accident` IS `situation`
        `date the injured person reaches pension age`      IS `pension age`
        `the injured person has died`                      IS FALSE
        `an insurer has paid damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim` IS `damages paid`
        `limitations`                                      IS `the limitations`

GIVEN `applied`      IS A DATE
      `exceptional`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `anticipated`  IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Application facts`
`my application facts` `applied` `exceptional` `anticipated` MEANS
    `Application facts` WITH
        `date of the application`                                                    IS `applied`
        `the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify earlier payment` IS `exceptional`
        `date the person anticipated returning to paid work, or starting work or a business` IS `anticipated`

§§ `Applying for defined benefits (ss 55, 58, 59, 60, 65)`

@export May I apply for defined benefits under the ACT motor accident injuries scheme (s 55)?
GIVEN `I was injured in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured in the motor accident
      `I am a dependant of someone who died as a result of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a dependant (a dependent child, a domestic partner or a financially dependent former domestic partner) of someone who died as a result of the accident
      `I paid, or must pay, the funeral expenses of someone who died as a result of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid, or are liable to pay, the funeral expenses of someone who died as a result of the accident
      `I am the guardian of one of those people who has a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the guardian of such a person who is a child or not legally competent to apply
      `I am the personal representative of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold probate or letters of administration for the person who died (or are an executor by representation or the public trustee and guardian), applying for the dependants
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for defined benefits` IF
    `may make an application for defined benefits under s 55` `I was injured in the accident` `I am a dependant of someone who died as a result of the accident` `I paid, or must pay, the funeral expenses of someone who died as a result of the accident` `I am the guardian of one of those people who has a legal disability` `I am the personal representative of the person who died`

@export By when must I apply for defined benefits: the last day of the 13-week application period (ss 58, 59 (1))?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS A `Benefits applied for` @desc Which defined benefits you are applying for: income replacement or treatment and care benefits (you were injured), death benefits (you are a dependant or the personal representative), or funeral benefits (you paid or must pay for the funeral)
      `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc For death or funeral benefits, the date the injured person died (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply` IS
    `the last day of the application period beginning on` (`the first day of the application period for` `what I am applying for` `after an accident on` `the date of the accident` `and a death on` `the date of the death`)

@export If I miss the application period, what is the last day on which the insurer may accept a late application (s 59 (2) (a))?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS A `Benefits applied for` @desc Which defined benefits you are applying for: income replacement or treatment and care benefits, death benefits, or funeral benefits
      `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc For death or funeral benefits, the date the injured person died (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day for a late application` IS
    `the last day for a late application for` `what I am applying for` `after an accident on` `the date of the accident` `and a death on` `the date of the death`

@export Is my application in time; if it is late, may the insurer accept it, and is it taken to have accepted it (s 59)?
GIVEN `what I am applying for` IS A `Benefits applied for` @desc Which defined benefits you are applying for: income replacement or treatment and care benefits, death benefits, or funeral benefits
      `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc For death or funeral benefits, the date the injured person died (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your application for defined benefits to the insurer (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the insurer received my explanation for the delay` IS A DATE @desc For a late application, the date the insurer received your explanation of why you applied late (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date you applied
      `the insurer's response to my explanation` IS A `Response to a late application` @desc Whether the insurer has responded to your explanation for the late application: no response yet, accepted, or refused
      `the date of the insurer's response` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer responded to your explanation (YYYY-MM-DD); if it has not responded, give today's date
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked about, usually today (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
DECIDE `Is my application in time` IS
    `the s 59 timing of the application` `what I am applying for` `the date of the accident` `the date of the death` `the date I applied` `the date the insurer received my explanation for the delay` `the insurer's response to my explanation` `the date of the insurer's response` `the day I am asking about`

@export By when must the insurer give me a receipt notice for my application (s 60 (1))?
GIVEN `the date the insurer received my application` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer received your application for defined benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the days the MAI guidelines allow for a receipt notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after receiving an application that the MAI guidelines allow the insurer for a receipt notice (the guidelines are not part of this encoding; check the current MAI guidelines)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the insurer give me a receipt notice` IS
    `the last day for the receipt notice` `the date the insurer received my application` `the days the MAI guidelines allow for a receipt notice`

@export By when must the insurer decide whether it accepts liability for my defined benefits (s 65 (1))?
GIVEN `the date of my receipt notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the receipt notice (or late receipt notice) the insurer gave you for your application (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the insurer decide liability` IS
    `the last day to decide liability after a receipt notice on` `the date of my receipt notice`

@export Has the insurer accepted liability for my defined benefits, or is it taken to have accepted it because it did not reject or transfer my application within 28 days (s 65)?
GIVEN `the date of my receipt notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the receipt notice (or late receipt notice) the insurer gave you for your application (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the notice the insurer has given me about liability` IS A `Decision on liability so far` @desc Which notice about liability the insurer has given you, if any: none yet, a defined benefits notice (accepting), a transfer notice (another insurer is liable), or a rejection notice
      `the date of that notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the insurer's notice about liability (YYYY-MM-DD); if none has been given, give today's date
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked about, usually today (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Liability position`
DECIDE `Has the insurer accepted liability` IS
    `the s 65 liability position` `the date of my receipt notice` `the notice the insurer has given me about liability` `the date of that notice` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Income replacement benefits (part 2.4) -- if the injury keeps you from your usual paid work`

@export Am I entitled to income replacement benefits (ss 78, 79, 89 to 92, and the limitations in ss 43 to 50)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `my age on the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the date of the motor accident
      `my work situation on the date of the accident` IS A `Work situation` @desc Your situation on the date of the accident: in paid work (as an ongoing or fixed-term employee, self-employed, or a casual worker with or without 260 hours in the year before), not working but with 260 hours in the year before, receiving workers compensation or MAI weekly payments, on unpaid leave expecting to return, with a new job or business arranged, a full-time student expecting paid work, or none of these
      `the date I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The date you reach, or reached, pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), s 23 (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an insurer has already paid you damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim (a common law claim) for this accident
      `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle in the accident, and none of these applies: another vehicle involved was insured and its insurer is the relevant insurer; it was a single-vehicle no-fault accident; you drove believing on reasonable grounds that the vehicle was insured and that its responsible person consented
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence (s 41) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left (or the MAI commission has declared you not entitled because of diplomatic immunity)
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `I am a detainee or young detainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, for the period asked about, a detainee (Corrections Management Act 2007) or a young detainee (Children and Young People Act 2008)
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence in relation to the accident (s 48 (6): for example murder, manslaughter, culpable driving, level 4 drink driving, refusing a breath test, drug driving, menacing driving), with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer in writing that the accident was caused by, or attributable to, an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claimed workers compensation for the injury and the claim was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks of the accident, nor rejected)
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` IS
    `the entitlement to income replacement benefits of` (`my facts as an injured person` `the date of the accident` `my age on the date of the accident` `my work situation on the date of the accident` `the date I reach pension age` `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` `the limitations`)
    WHERE
        -- s 43 (3) does not bear on income replacement benefits: FALSE.
        `the limitations` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` FALSE `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` `I am a detainee or young detainee` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`

@export Which income replacement payment period is this day in: the first (13 weeks from the accident) or the second (to 5 years after it) (s 93)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is asked about (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `Payment period`
DECIDE `Which payment period is this day in` IS
    `the payment period of` `the day I am asking about` `after an accident on` `the date of the accident`

@export From when, and until when, are my income replacement benefits payable (s 101, with s 51)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `my age on the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the date of the motor accident
      `my work situation on the date of the accident` IS A `Work situation` @desc Your situation on the date of the accident: in paid work (as an ongoing or fixed-term employee, self-employed, or a casual worker with or without 260 hours in the year before), not working but with 260 hours in the year before, receiving workers compensation or MAI weekly payments, on unpaid leave expecting to return, with a new job or business arranged, a full-time student expecting paid work, or none of these
      `the date I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The date you reach, or reached, pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), s 23 (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an insurer has already paid you damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim (a common law claim) for this accident
      `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle in the accident, and none of the s 43 (2) exceptions applies
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `I am a detainee or young detainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, for the period asked about, a detainee or a young detainee
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence (s 48 (6)) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your workers compensation claim for the injury was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks, nor rejected)
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your application for defined benefits to the insurer (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late application, whether the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify paying from the earlier date (answer no if your application was in time)
      `the date I expected to return to work or start work` IS A DATE @desc If you were on unpaid leave, had a new job or business arranged, or were a full-time student: the date you expected to return to paid work or start the work or business (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
GIVETH A `Period answer`
DECIDE `When are my income replacement benefits payable` IS
    `the period for which income replacement benefits are payable` (`my facts as an injured person` `the date of the accident` `my age on the date of the accident` `my work situation on the date of the accident` `the date I reach pension age` `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` `the limitations`) (`my application facts` `the date I applied` `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` `the date I expected to return to work or start work`)
    WHERE
        -- s 43 (3) does not bear on income replacement benefits: FALSE.
        `the limitations` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` FALSE `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` `I am a detainee or young detainee` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`

@export How much income replacement benefit do I get for the week that includes this day, and for the fortnight's payment (ss 96, 97, 98, 101, 102)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc A day in the week the payment is for (YYYY-MM-DD); the AWE indexed amounts of that day are used (deposited for 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)
      `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `my age on the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the date of the motor accident
      `my work situation on the date of the accident` IS A `Work situation` @desc Your situation on the date of the accident: in paid work (as an ongoing or fixed-term employee, self-employed, or a casual worker with or without 260 hours in the year before), not working but with 260 hours in the year before, receiving workers compensation or MAI weekly payments, on unpaid leave expecting to return, with a new job or business arranged, a full-time student expecting paid work, or none of these
      `the date I reach pension age` IS A DATE @desc The date you reach, or reached, pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cwlth), s 23 (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957) (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an insurer has already paid you damages for loss of income under a motor accident claim (a common law claim) for this accident
      `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle in the accident, and none of the s 43 (2) exceptions applies
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `I am a detainee or young detainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, for the period asked about, a detainee or a young detainee
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence (s 48 (6)) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your workers compensation claim for the injury was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks, nor rejected)
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your application for defined benefits to the insurer (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late application, whether the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify paying from the earlier date (answer no if your application was in time)
      `the date I expected to return to work or start work` IS A DATE @desc If you were on unpaid leave, had a new job or business arranged, or were a full-time student: the date you expected to return to paid work or start the work or business (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
      `my pre-injury weekly income, AWE adjusted` IS A NUMBER @desc Your pre-injury weekly income (or pre-injury earning capacity) in Australian dollars, as the insurer works it out under ss 80 to 88 (usually the average weekly gross pay, or net self-employed income, over the 52 weeks before the accident), adjusted for AWE growth under s 94 since the accident
      `my post-injury earning capacity a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What the insurer has decided you can now earn a week in work you are suited to (s 100), in Australian dollars; 0 if you cannot work at all
      `my employer paid superannuation for me in the 52 weeks before the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employer paid, or had to pay, superannuation contributions for you in the 52 weeks before the accident
      `the superannuation guarantee charge percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The superannuation guarantee charge percentage for the year the contributions were paid or payable, which s 96 (2) takes from the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Cwlth), s 19 (2) (12 for 2025-26 and 11.5 for 2024-25; from 1 July 2026 that Act sets 12 in s 17A (2))
      `the workers compensation I receive for that week` IS A NUMBER @desc Any weekly workers compensation payment for loss of income you receive for that week, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Income replacement answer`
DECIDE `How much income replacement benefit do I get` IS
    `the income replacement benefit for the week of` `the day I am asking about` `for` (`my facts as an injured person` `the date of the accident` `my age on the date of the accident` `my work situation on the date of the accident` `the date I reach pension age` `an insurer has already paid me damages for loss of income` `the limitations`) (`my application facts` `the date I applied` `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` `the date I expected to return to work or start work`) `the figures`
    WHERE
        -- s 43 (3) does not bear on income replacement benefits: FALSE.
        `the limitations` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle in the accident, with no s 43 (2) exception` FALSE `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` `I am a detainee or young detainee` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`
        `the figures` MEANS
            `Income replacement figures` WITH
                `pre-injury income AWE adjusted`                                        IS `my pre-injury weekly income, AWE adjusted`
                `post-injury earning capacity`                                          IS `my post-injury earning capacity a week`
                `employer superannuation contributions paid or payable in the 52 weeks before the accident` IS `my employer paid superannuation for me in the 52 weeks before the accident`
                `superannuation guarantee charge percentage for the year of the contributions` IS `the superannuation guarantee charge percentage`
                `workers compensation payment for the week`                             IS `the workers compensation I receive for that week`

@export How much may the insurer pay me as an interim weekly payment while it waits for information it asked me for (s 103)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the insurer asked me for more information` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer asked you for the additional information it needs to work out your income replacement benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I have given the insurer that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the insurer the information it asked for
      `the date I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The date you gave the insurer the information (YYYY-MM-DD); if you have not, give today's date
      `the percentage prescribed by regulation` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of $2 250 AWE indexed that the regulations prescribe for an interim weekly payment (the regulation is not part of this encoding; for example 80 for 80%)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day the payment is for (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `How much interim weekly payment may the insurer pay me` IS
    `the interim weekly payment` `the percentage prescribed by regulation` `on` `the day I am asking about` `ending` (`the last day for interim weekly payments` `the date of the accident` `the date the insurer asked me for more information` `I have given the insurer that information` `the date I gave it`)

@export Until when may the insurer pay me interim weekly payments (s 103 (2))?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date the insurer asked me for more information` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer asked you for the additional information it needs to work out your income replacement benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I have given the insurer that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the insurer the information it asked for
      `the date I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The date you gave the insurer the information (YYYY-MM-DD); if you have not, give today's date
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when may I get interim weekly payments` IS
    `the last day for interim weekly payments` `the date of the accident` `the date the insurer asked me for more information` `I have given the insurer that information` `the date I gave it`

§§ `Treatment and care benefits (part 2.5): entitlement and period only`

@export Am I entitled to treatment and care benefits (s 112, with ss 45, 47 to 50 and 118)?
GIVEN `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `I am a detainee or young detainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, for the period asked about, a detainee or a young detainee
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence (s 48 (6)) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your workers compensation claim for the injury was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks, nor rejected)
      `I am a participant in the LTCS scheme for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the lifetime care and support (LTCS) scheme for a catastrophic injury from the accident
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to treatment and care benefits` IS
    `the entitlement to treatment and care benefits` `the limitations` `I am a participant in the LTCS scheme for the injury`
    WHERE
        -- Only ss 45, 47, 48, 49 and 50 bear on treatment and care benefits (s 112 (2)); the others are FALSE.
        `the limitations` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` FALSE `I am a detainee or young detainee` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`

@export For what period are my treatment and care benefits payable (s 128)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you made your application for defined benefits to the insurer (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late application, whether the insurer is satisfied on reasonable grounds that exceptional circumstances justify paying from the date of the accident (answer no if your application was in time)
GIVETH A `Period answer`
DECIDE `When are my treatment and care benefits payable` IS
    `the period for which treatment and care benefits are payable` `the date of the accident` (`my application facts` `the date I applied` `the insurer accepts there are exceptional circumstances for earlier payment` `the date of the accident`)

§§ `Quality of life benefits (part 2.6), and whether I can sue (s 239) -- once your injuries have been assessed for whole person impairment (WPI)`

@export Am I entitled to quality of life benefits (ss 132 to 136, and the limitations in ss 43 to 50)?
GIVEN `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `I was a child on the date of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) on the date of the accident
      `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, 4 years and 6 months after the accident, you were receiving treatment and care benefits for the injury and met the requirements in the regulations, or were a participant in the LTCS scheme
      `I am a foreign national living permanently outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are neither an Australian citizen nor a permanent resident, and live permanently outside Australia
      `I have already received quality of life benefits for the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already received quality of life benefits for this accident
      `I have been awarded quality of life damages for the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has awarded you quality of life damages in a motor accident claim for this accident
      `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle, and no other vehicle was insured with the relevant insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle in the accident and no other vehicle involved was insured by an insurer that is the relevant insurer (s 43 (3))
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence (s 48 (6)) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your workers compensation claim for the injury was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks, nor rejected)
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to quality of life benefits` IS
    `the entitlement to quality of life benefits of` (`my quality of life facts` `my WPI` `I was a child on the date of the accident` `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant` `I am a foreign national living permanently outside Australia` `I have already received quality of life benefits for the accident` `I have been awarded quality of life damages for the accident` `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle, and no other vehicle was insured with the relevant insurer` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`)

-- The quality of life facts from plain answers. Sections 43 (2) and 47 do not bear on quality of life benefits
-- (s 132 (2)): FALSE.
GIVEN `wpi` IS A NUMBER
      `child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at 4 years 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `already received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `damages awarded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `uninsured (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `two offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `self` IS A BOOLEAN
      `serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `terror` IS A BOOLEAN
      `workers comp` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Quality of life facts`
`my quality of life facts` `wpi` `child` `at 4 years 6 months` `foreign` `already received` `damages awarded` `uninsured (3)` `one offence` `two offences` `self` `serious` `terror` `workers comp` MEANS
    `Quality of life facts` WITH
        `WPI assessed`                                                   IS `wpi`
        `a child on the date of the motor accident`                      IS `child`
        `4 years 6 months after the accident, receiving treatment and care benefits and meeting the prescribed requirements, or an LTCS scheme participant` IS `at 4 years 6 months`
        `a foreign national living permanently outside Australia`        IS `foreign`
        `has already received quality of life benefits for the accident` IS `already received`
        `has been awarded quality of life damages for the accident`      IS `damages awarded`
        `limitations` IS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE `uninsured (3)` `one offence` `two offences` `self` FALSE `serious` `terror` `workers comp`

@export Once the insurer has accepted liability, between which dates may I apply for quality of life benefits (s 137 (2))?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH AN `Application window`
DECIDE `When may I apply for quality of life benefits` IS
    `the quality of life application window after an accident on` `the date of the accident`

@export How much quality of life benefit does my WPI give me (s 167, table 167)?
GIVEN `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `the date of my WPI report` IS A DATE @desc The date of your WPI report (the later one if physical and psychological injuries were reported on separately; or the date of a notice affirming or increasing it on review) (YYYY-MM-DD); the AWE indexed amounts of that day are used
      `I was a child on the date of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) on the date of the accident
      `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, 4 years and 6 months after the accident, you were receiving treatment and care benefits for the injury and met the requirements in the regulations, or were a participant in the LTCS scheme
      `I am a foreign national living permanently outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are neither an Australian citizen nor a permanent resident, and live permanently outside Australia
      `I have already received quality of life benefits for the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already received quality of life benefits for this accident
      `I have been awarded quality of life damages for the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has awarded you quality of life damages in a motor accident claim for this accident
      `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle, and no other vehicle was insured with the relevant insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the driver or responsible person of an uninsured vehicle in the accident and no other vehicle involved was insured by an insurer that is the relevant insurer (s 43 (3))
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence (s 48 (6)) in relation to the accident, with no appeal left
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your workers compensation claim for the injury was accepted or settled (and not withdrawn within 13 weeks, nor rejected)
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `How much quality of life benefit do I get` IS
    `the quality of life benefits payable` (`my quality of life facts` `my WPI` `I was a child on the date of the accident` `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant` `I am a foreign national living permanently outside Australia` `I have already received quality of life benefits for the accident` `I have been awarded quality of life damages for the accident` `I drove or was responsible for an uninsured vehicle, and no other vehicle was insured with the relevant insurer` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a driving offence over the accident` `I have been convicted or found guilty of 2 or more driving offences over the accident` `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` `I have been convicted or found guilty of a serious offence over the accident` `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` `my workers compensation claim for the injury has been accepted or settled`) `the date of my WPI report`

@export Once my WPI has been assessed, which section applies and what must the insurer offer me (ss 154 to 157)?
GIVEN `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than you (for example the at-fault driver, through their insurer) is liable to you in damages for the injury, so that you are entitled to make a motor accident claim (a common law claim)
GIVETH A `WPI notice section`
DECIDE `What must the insurer offer me` IS
    `the WPI notice section for` `my WPI` `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury`

@export By when must the insurer give me its notice about my WPI report (ss 154 (3), 155 (4), 156 (4), 157 (4))?
GIVEN `the date the insurer received my WPI report` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer received your WPI report (the later one if physical and psychological injuries were reported on separately) (YYYY-MM-DD)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the insurer give me the WPI notice` IS
    `the last day for the WPI notice` `the date the insurer received my WPI report`

@export By when must I tell the insurer whether I accept or disagree with my WPI report (ss 154 to 157)?
GIVEN `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than you is liable to you in damages for the injury, so that you are entitled to make a motor accident claim
      `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date I received the insurer's WPI notice` IS A DATE @desc The date you received the insurer's notice with your WPI report (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I gave a complying notice of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given a complying notice of claim for a motor accident claim (s 257)
      `the date my claim was finally decided` IS A DATE @desc If you gave a complying notice of claim, the date the claim was finally decided (YYYY-MM-DD); otherwise give the date of the accident
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I reply to the WPI notice` IS
    `the last day to reply to the WPI notice` (`the WPI notice section for` `my WPI` `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury`) `the date of the accident` `the date I received the insurer's WPI notice` `I gave a complying notice of claim` `the date my claim was finally decided`

@export If I do not reply to the insurer's WPI notice in time, what happens (ss 154 (4), 155 (5), 156 (5), 157 (6))?
GIVEN `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed (the higher one if physical and psychological injuries were assessed separately)
      `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than you is liable to you in damages for the injury, so that you are entitled to make a motor accident claim
      `the insurer made me an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer's WPI notice offered you an amount of quality of life benefits
GIVETH A `Silence on the WPI notice`
DECIDE `What happens if I do not reply to the WPI notice` IS
    `what silence on the WPI notice means` (`the WPI notice section for` `my WPI` `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury`) `the insurer made me an offer`

@export Does my WPI let me sue for damages in a motor accident claim (s 239; ss 156, 157)? Damages themselves are not worked out here.
GIVEN `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone other than you (for example the at-fault driver, through their insurer) is liable to you in damages for the injury
      `I have made a quality of life benefits application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a quality of life benefits application (s 137)
      `my WPI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your whole person impairment from the accident, as a whole number percentage, as assessed by an independent medical examiner (or the insurer's final offer WPI; or, for a foreign national paid a lump sum, as assessed by a private medical examiner)
      `I am a foreign national paid a lump sum under s 184 (6), assessed by a private medical examiner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a foreign national who received a lump sum under s 184 (6) and whose WPI was assessed by a private medical examiner under the WPI assessment guidelines
      `I was a child on the date of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) on the date of the accident
      `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, 4 years and 6 months after the accident, you were receiving treatment and care benefits for the injury and met the requirements in the regulations, or were a participant in the LTCS scheme
      `an SOI report found my injury has a significant occupational impact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taken to have a WPI of 10% because an SOI report found your injury has a significant occupational impact (s 213 (2) (a))
      `I made a successful workers compensation claim for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a workers compensation claim for the injury at least 26 weeks before your notice of claim or WPI assessment, and it was accepted or settled and not withdrawn (s 239 (4))
GIVETH A `Motor accident claim answer`
DECIDE `Can I sue for damages` IS
    `the s 239 answer` (`Motor accident claim facts` WITH
        `someone other than the injured person is liable in damages for the injury` IS `someone else is liable to me in damages for the injury`
        `has made a quality of life benefits application`                            IS `I have made a quality of life benefits application`
        `WPI assessed, or the insurer's final offer WPI`                             IS `my WPI`
        `a foreign national paid a s 184 (6) lump sum and assessed by a private medical examiner` IS `I am a foreign national paid a lump sum under s 184 (6), assessed by a private medical examiner`
        `taken to have a WPI of 10% under s 133`                                      IS `I was a child on the date of the accident` AND `4 years and 6 months after the accident, I was receiving treatment and care benefits and met the prescribed requirements, or was an LTCS participant`
        `taken to have a WPI of 10% because of a significant occupational impact (s 213 (2) (a))` IS `an SOI report found my injury has a significant occupational impact`
        `has made a successful claim for workers compensation benefits for the injury` IS `I made a successful workers compensation claim for the injury`
        -- s 239 (1) (e): the person asking is alive; the claim after a death (s 228 (b)) is not encoded.
        `has died as a result of the accident`                                        IS FALSE)

§§ `Death benefits (part 2.7) -- if someone died as a result of a motor accident`

@export Am I a dependant of the person who died, for death benefits (s 168)?
GIVEN `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship to the person who died` @desc How you were related to the person who died: their child (including one born after the death), their grandchild or step child, their domestic partner, their former domestic partner, or none of these
      `I lived with the person as a member of their family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived with the person as a member of their family when they died (matters for a grandchild or step child)
      `my age when the person died` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the person died
      `I was a full-time student when the person died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a full-time student when the person died
      `I am a person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person with a disability (Disability Services Act 1991)
      `I was wholly or partly financially dependent on the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were wholly or partly financially dependent on the person when they died
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dependant of the person who died` IF
    `is a dependant under s 168` (`Dependant facts` WITH
        `relationship`                                              IS `my relationship to the person who died`
        `living with the person as a member of the person's family` IS `I lived with the person as a member of their family`
        `age when the person died`                                  IS `my age when the person died`
        `a full-time student when the person died`                  IS `I was a full-time student when the person died`
        `a person with a disability`                                IS `I am a person with a disability`
        `wholly or partly financially dependent on the person`      IS `I was wholly or partly financially dependent on the person`)

@export What death benefits are payable to the dependants of the person who died (ss 36, 169 to 174)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `on the date of the accident the person had a domestic partner or a dependent former domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the date of the accident, the person who died had a domestic partner, or a former domestic partner who was wholly or partly financially dependent on them
      `the number of dependent children on the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children (s 168 (2)) the person who died had on the date of the accident
      `the death was from an intentionally self-inflicted injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death was caused by an intentionally self-inflicted injury
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `the person was a foreign national who died outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was neither an Australian citizen nor a permanent resident, and died outside Australia
      `a coroner found conduct making up 2 or more driving offences or a serious offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coroner established that the person's conduct in the accident made up the physical elements of 2 or more driving offences or a serious offence
      `the person received quality of life benefits or damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died had received quality of life benefits or quality of life damages for the accident
      `death benefits have been paid under workers compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether death benefits (other than funeral expenses) have been paid under a workers compensation scheme for the death
      `the day the benefits are worked out` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the death benefits are worked out, for example the date of the ACAT order (YYYY-MM-DD); the AWE indexed amounts of that day are used
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `What death benefits are payable` IS
    `the death benefits payable to the dependants` (`Death facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                                          IS `the date of the accident`
        `date of death`                                                       IS `the date of the death`
        `had a domestic partner or dependent former domestic partner on the date of the motor accident` IS `on the date of the accident the person had a domestic partner or a dependent former domestic partner`
        `number of dependent children on the date of the motor accident`      IS `the number of dependent children on the date of the accident`
        `the death was caused by an intentionally self-inflicted injury`      IS `the death was from an intentionally self-inflicted injury`
        `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism`
        `a foreign national whose death happened outside Australia`           IS `the person was a foreign national who died outside Australia`
        `a coroner established conduct making up 2 or more driving offences or a serious offence` IS `a coroner found conduct making up 2 or more driving offences or a serious offence`
        `the person who died received quality of life benefits or damages`    IS `the person received quality of life benefits or damages`
        `death benefits were paid under a workers compensation scheme`        IS `death benefits have been paid under workers compensation`) `the day the benefits are worked out`

@export From what day may the insurer apply to the ACAT for the order paying our death benefits (s 176 (3))?
GIVEN `the date the insurer accepted liability for the death benefits` IS A DATE @desc The date the insurer accepted liability for the application for death benefits (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the number of ACT public holidays on weekdays in the 5 business days after that` IS A NUMBER @desc How many ACT public holidays fall on a weekday in the business days counted after that date (usually 0)
      `the insurer asked a dependant for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer gave a dependant notice asking for additional information about the application
      `the date it asked` IS A DATE @desc The date of that notice (YYYY-MM-DD); if none, give the date the insurer accepted liability
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From when may the insurer apply to the ACAT for our death benefits` IS
    `the first day the insurer may apply to the ACAT` `the date the insurer accepted liability for the death benefits` `the number of ACT public holidays on weekdays in the 5 business days after that` `the insurer asked a dependant for more information` `the date it asked`

@export Must the insurer pay the estate the income replacement and treatment and care benefits the person was owed when they died, without recovering what it paid (s 175)?
GIVEN `the insurer has accepted liability for the death benefits application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has accepted liability for an application for death benefits for the person who died
      `before dying, the person was entitled to income replacement or treatment and care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before dying, the person was entitled to income replacement benefits or treatment and care benefits
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the estate paid what the person was owed` IF
    `the estate must be paid the benefits owed and not received, and nothing paid is recovered (s 175)` `the insurer has accepted liability for the death benefits application` `before dying, the person was entitled to income replacement or treatment and care benefits`

§§ `Funeral benefits (part 2.8) -- if you paid, or must pay, for the funeral of someone who died as a result of a motor accident`

@export How much funeral benefit can I be paid for the funeral of the person who died (ss 36, 178 to 181)?
GIVEN `the date of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The date of the motor accident (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc The date the person died (YYYY-MM-DD)
      `I paid, or must pay, the funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid, or are liable to pay, the funeral expenses of the person who died
      `the funeral costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses, in Australian dollars, including the cost of taking the body elsewhere in Australia or overseas (what counts is set by the MAI guidelines)
      `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the MAI commission has notified the insurer that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism
      `the person was a foreign national who died outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was neither an Australian citizen nor a permanent resident, and died outside Australia
      `the funeral expenses have been paid under workers compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the funeral expenses have been paid under a workers compensation scheme
      `the day the benefits are worked out` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the funeral benefits are worked out or paid (YYYY-MM-DD); the AWE indexed maximum of that day is used
GIVETH A `MAI amount answer`
DECIDE `How much funeral benefit can I be paid` IS
    `the funeral benefits payable` (`Funeral facts` WITH
        `date of the motor accident`                                          IS `the date of the accident`
        `date of death`                                                       IS `the date of the death`
        `has paid, or is liable to pay, the funeral expenses`                 IS `I paid, or must pay, the funeral expenses`
        `the funeral expenses`                                                IS `the funeral costs`
        `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was caused by an act of terrorism` IS `the MAI commission has notified that the accident was an act of terrorism`
        `a foreign national whose death happened outside Australia`           IS `the person was a foreign national who died outside Australia`
        `funeral expenses were paid under a workers compensation scheme`      IS `the funeral expenses have been paid under workers compensation`) `the day the benefits are worked out`
